TITLE:: REScore
summary:: A score: what you did to a song, as events in a JSON file
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScoreRecorder, Classes/RETap, Classes/REJSON

DESCRIPTION::
The events of a performance (inputs, actions on the reCurrent objects, code lines, snapshots) with the beat they happened on and the metadata that replays them, as one JSON file in the format of the reCording guide ("The take file"). Made by link::Classes/REScoreRecorder::, played by REScorePlayer, edited by its own methods.

Events are IdentityDictionaries kept in their file form: the fields code::kind::, code::voice::, code::method::, code::name::, code::key:: and code::msg:: are Symbols in memory and plain strings in the file; values go through the codec (link::#*encodeValue::, link::#*decodeValue::).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: song
An link::Classes/RCSong:: or its name.
argument:: piece
argument:: wersion

METHOD:: read
argument:: path
returns:: The score, nil (reported) for a missing file or another format.

METHOD:: fromDict
METHOD:: fromJSONString

METHOD:: pathFor
argument:: root
argument:: song
argument:: version
argument:: stamp
returns:: code::<root>/<stamp>_<song> <version>.json:: (link::Classes/RETake#*path::).

METHOD:: encodeValue
argument:: x
returns:: The file form of a value: numbers, strings, symbols, arrays as they are; an Event as an object, another Dictionary as code::{dict: ...}::; a Pattern, a Function with source, a Ref, an Env, a Rest, a Quant, a ControlSpec, an Association, a Char, a Class, a Point, a Rect, an Interval, a Tuning or a Scale as code::{sc: <compile string>}::; a reCurrent object as its reference (link::#*rcRef::); anything else as code::{ref: <print string>}::.

METHOD:: encode
argument:: x
returns:: code::[encoded, replayable]::: false when a code::{ref}:: appears anywhere inside.

METHOD:: decodeValue
argument:: x
argument:: song
The song references are resolved through (the default session's, by the reference's song name, when nil).
returns:: The value back: code::{sc}:: compiled and run (nil, reported, when it does not compile or raises), code::{rc}:: resolved (left as the reference when it cannot be), code::{ref}:: as it is, objects as Events.

METHOD:: rcRef
argument:: obj
returns:: code::{rc: "beat"|"layer"|"song"|"batch"|"orgnsm"|"fobject"|"crawler", name: ..., layer: ..., song: ...}::, nil for anything else.

METHOD:: resolve
argument:: ref
argument:: song
returns:: The live object: beats, layers, orgnsms and fobjects through the song; batches and crawlers through the current (then the top) environment, by the variable holding them.

METHOD:: isRef

METHOD:: gitHead
argument:: dir
returns:: The short commit of the checkout holding dir, nil outside one.

METHOD:: keyOrder
The field order of the file.

METHOD:: merge
argument:: a
argument:: b
The overdub take.
argument:: voices
The overdubbed voices (nil: every voice of b).
argument:: mode
code::\replace:: drops a's events of those voices within punch; code::\keep:: drops nothing; code::\touch:: drops a's events of each control b touched between b's first and last touch of it; nil is touch for continuous controls and replace for the voice's other events.
argument:: punch
code::[in, out]:: (out nil: b's duration).
argument:: loopSpan
code::[from, to]:: when b was recorded over a loop: its beats fold into the span and, unless keep, only the last pass of each voice (each control for touch and auto) remains.
returns:: A copy of a with b merged in (ids renewed, causes following), the overdub noted in code::meta[\overdubs]::.

METHOD:: controlKey
argument:: e
returns:: What an event controls: code::[\midi, name]::, code::[\osc, key]::, code::[\set | \rPut | \setArg, objectName, key]::, code::[\cc, device, num]::, code::[\bend | \touch, device, chan]::; nil for a note, a transport action, a code line.

METHOD:: controlValue
METHOD:: isContinuous
argument:: e
A control that sets a number.

