subsection:: Editing

Every operation answers a new score and leaves the receiver as it was; ids are kept; beats and seconds move together through the tempo map (link::#-beatsToSecs::). code::voices:: and code::kinds:: restrict an operation (nil: all).

METHOD:: shifted
argument:: beats
Negative undoes a latency. What lands before 0 is dropped (reported); a snapshot there is kept at 0.
argument:: voices
argument:: kinds
METHOD:: scaled
argument:: factor
argument:: voices
argument:: kinds
argument:: origin
The beat the stretch is around.
METHOD:: quantized
argument:: grid
Beats.
argument:: voices
argument:: kinds
argument:: strength
1 moves to the grid, 0.5 half the way.
METHOD:: retimed
argument:: func
code::{ |beat, event| newBeat }::.
argument:: voices
argument:: kinds
METHOD:: trimmed
argument:: from
argument:: to
The events of [from, to) rebased to 0, the latest snapshot before from kept at 0 and leading, the tempo map rebased.
METHOD:: thinned
argument:: tolerance
A point of a continuous control within it of the line between its kept neighbours goes; the ends and the corners stay.
argument:: voices
METHOD:: smoothed
argument:: window
Points, odd, centred; the values of the continuous controls averaged.
argument:: voices
METHOD:: withoutVoices
METHOD:: onlyVoices
argument:: voices
METHOD:: withoutKinds
argument:: kinds
METHOD:: renamedVoice
argument:: old
argument:: new
METHOD:: replacedSegment
argument:: controlKey
argument:: from
argument:: to
argument:: points
code::[[beat, value], ...]:: shaped like the control's first recorded event (what a curve editor sends).
METHOD:: valueAt
argument:: controlKey
argument:: beat
The control's value at a beat: its last point at or before it, else its first.
METHOD:: beatsToSecs
argument:: beat
Through the tempo map (piecewise constant).

EXAMPLES::

code::
s = REScore.read(~piece_dir +/+ "Scores/261001_143012_demo w1.json");
s.voiceNames;
s.eventsOf('core/kick').collect { |e| [e[\beat], e[\method], e[\args]] };
REScore.decodeValue(s.at(2)[\args], ~song);
::
